    "difficultyReason": "A single unscaffolded direct-proportion task. The student must set up m = kl, find k = 9 ÷ 2.5 = 3.6 (a clean decimal division), then substitute l = 4. That is two linked routine steps with no reframing or interpretation. It is harder than p16-q3, which gives the variable relationship symbolically and splits the work into parts. It is easier than p19-q4, where k is the awkward fraction 3/28 and the context is less direct.",
